From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 16:30:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 137/143] config: enable nftables, iptables NAT/MASQUERADE and
 WireGuard
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A user running this kernel as a small router/VPN box reported that the
config has no way to do NAT or run a VPN (github issue #4): NF_TABLES and
NF_NAT were unset, so neither nft nor iptables could set up masquerading,
and there was no WireGuard.

NETFILTER, NF_CONNTRACK and IP_NF_IPTABLES were already enabled, but the
tables themselves were missing. Add both userspace paths:

  - nftables (NF_TABLES + inet family, ct/log/limit/masq/redir/nat/fib
    expressions) and NFT_COMPAT, which is what iptables-nft — the default
    iptables backend in Debian 13 and Ubuntu — needs;
  - the legacy xtables path (NETFILTER_XTABLES_LEGACY), which since v6.12
    is what gates IP_NF_FILTER/IP_NF_NAT/IP_NF_TARGET_MASQUERADE, so
    iptables-legacy scripts keep working too.

NF_NAT, NF_NAT_MASQUERADE, NETFILTER_XT_NAT and the crypto library bits
WireGuard needs are pulled in automatically.

Everything is a module except the bool gates, so the Image is unchanged
and nothing loads unless the administrator configures it.

While here, add the eight IR protocol decoders that were enabled in the
.config the shipped kernels were built from but had never been written
back to the versioned defconfig. RC_CORE, IR_SUNXI and IR_GPIO_CIR were
already there; without the decoders a receiver wired to the header
(the board itself has none) would produce no scancodes.

Verified with a defconfig -> .config roundtrip: no option that was set in
the 6.18.44 build loses its value.

Link: https://github.com/ut-slayer/orangepi-4a-mainline/issues/4
Reported-by: ascold113 <https://github.com/ascold113>
Co-Authored-By: AI Agent
---
 arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig | 26 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig
index e71c2202b..948ff0a7a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig
@@ -92,14 +92,31 @@ CONFIG_NETFILTER=y
 CONFIG_BRIDGE_NETFILTER=m
 CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK=m
 CONFIG_NF_CONNTRACK_EVENTS=y
+CONFIG_NF_TABLES=m
+CONFIG_NF_TABLES_INET=y
+CONFIG_NFT_CT=m
+CONFIG_NFT_LOG=m
+CONFIG_NFT_LIMIT=m
+CONFIG_NFT_MASQ=m
+CONFIG_NFT_REDIR=m
+CONFIG_NFT_NAT=m
+CONFIG_NFT_COMPAT=m
+CONFIG_NETFILTER_XTABLES_LEGACY=y
 CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MARK=m
 CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_TARGET_LOG=m
 CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_ADDRTYPE=m
 CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_CONNTRACK=m
 CONFIG_NETFILTER_XT_MATCH_IPVS=m
 CONFIG_IP_VS=m
+CONFIG_NFT_FIB_IPV4=m
 CONFIG_IP_NF_IPTABLES=m
+CONFIG_IP_NF_TARGET_REJECT=m
+CONFIG_IP_NF_NAT=m
+CONFIG_IP_NF_TARGET_MASQUERADE=m
+CONFIG_NFT_FIB_IPV6=m
 CONFIG_IP6_NF_IPTABLES=m
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_NAT=m
+CONFIG_IP6_NF_TARGET_MASQUERADE=m
 CONFIG_BRIDGE=m
 CONFIG_BRIDGE_VLAN_FILTERING=y
 CONFIG_NET_DSA=m
@@ -242,6 +259,7 @@ CONFIG_BLK_DEV_DM=m
 CONFIG_DM_MIRROR=m
 CONFIG_DM_ZERO=m
 CONFIG_NETDEVICES=y
+CONFIG_WIREGUARD=m
 CONFIG_MACVLAN=m
 CONFIG_MACVTAP=m
 CONFIG_TUN=y
@@ -550,6 +568,14 @@ CONFIG_REGULATOR_TPS65219=y
 CONFIG_REGULATOR_VCTRL=m
 CONFIG_RC_CORE=m
 CONFIG_RC_DECODERS=y
+CONFIG_IR_JVC_DECODER=m
+CONFIG_IR_MCE_KBD_DECODER=m
+CONFIG_IR_NEC_DECODER=m
+CONFIG_IR_RC5_DECODER=m
+CONFIG_IR_RC6_DECODER=m
+CONFIG_IR_SANYO_DECODER=m
+CONFIG_IR_SHARP_DECODER=m
+CONFIG_IR_SONY_DECODER=m
 CONFIG_RC_DEVICES=y
 CONFIG_IR_GPIO_CIR=m
 CONFIG_IR_SUNXI=m
